      "q": "Which federal agency spends the most on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense spends the most on contracts. The Department of Defense obligated $303B in contracts through FY2026 to date, which is the largest single-agency total compared with other agencies such as the Department of Veterans Affairs at $70.1B and the Department of Homeland Security at $59.6B."
